    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` field so it returns `true` when an owner's city already holds **40\u201349 owners** (approaching the 50-owner hard limit), leaving the existing hard rejection at 50 unchanged.\n\nChanges, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` feature across the same layers:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `capacityWarning` boolean property (`readOnly`) to the owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets `getCapacityWarning`/`setCapacityWarning`.\n\n2. **`ClinicService.java`** \u2014 declared `boolean isCityCapacityWarningActive(String city)`.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 added `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40L` and implemented the method: reuses the existing `countOwnersInCity(...)` and returns `count >= 40 && count < CITY_OWNER_LIMIT (50)`. Null city \u2192 `false`.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 renamed the `withBulkSignupWarning` helper to `withDerivedWarnings`, which now sets both `bulkSignupWarning` and the city-specific `capacityWarning` (from `ownerDto.getCity()`); wired it into `getOwner`, `addOwner`, `updateOwner`, and `listOwners`.\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV2.java`** \u2014 set `capacityWarning` per owner in the paged listing for consistency.\n\nThe hard limit logic in `assertCityCapacity` (rejecting at \u2265 50 with `CityOwnerLimitException`) was left untouched.\n\nNote: this isn't a git repository, so no commit was made.",
